
-- Running command `help pmux_opt' --

    pmux_opt [-shiftx-small] [-flatten-fallback] [-const-decode] [-const-polarity] [-order-decode [-desc-order]] [-uniform-abc] [selection]

Remove constant-zero select arms and share identical data columns.
A one-arm cell remains a $pmux; B == A is not a removal condition.
-shiftx-small invokes upstream pmux2shiftx only for dense, mutually
exclusive 2/3-bit decoders covering all but at most one code point.
-flatten-fallback merges single-use nested fallback PMUXes using
a PMUX control gate, preserving unknown and multi-select semantics.
-const-decode propagates eq/logic_not selection predicates into
their own B arms only; A, S and the PMUX cell type remain intact.
-const-polarity complements only 0/1/X constant A/B tables and
adds a real output NOT; dynamic or Z-valued A/B are excluded.
-order-decode sorts B/S arms together by their constant decoder
value on the same control word. -desc-order selects descending
rather than ascending order. No arms are removed or combined.
-uniform-abc installs the same area-oriented ABC9 script for every
design, unless the caller has explicitly supplied abc9.script.

